            <div xml:id="d173">

                <pb facs="0220" n="1054" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1054"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/10027a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-04T19:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 4, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1185. For Sheldon [from
                        Fuller, War Trade
                    Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 1160. Frothingham. What progress has been made in matter
                    urging adoption effective enemy trade restrictions by Portugal? Portuguese in
                    certain South American countries are cloaking enemy <pb facs="0221" n="1055"
                        xml:id="pg1055"/> trade. Our representatives advise only effective remedy is
                    adoption of full enemy trade restrictions by Portugal. This should be discussed
                    with British in furtherance of early decision concerning publishing enemy
                    trading list for Portugal which was subject of communications from you several
                    months ago. French representative, Washington, has been instructed by his
                    Government to ask cooperation United States in obtaining British assistance
                    urging Portugal to act immediately. Await your advice as to situation. Fuller.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
